# dusk
## Dusk
The sun goes down behind the Janiculum as if it had a ship to catch, and you go back to the warehouse at a walk, with the dust of the day on your tunic, and your hands steady again, and the sound of the city in your ears like a very large tired animal.
?if b1.collis_start == "none"
  You have come home with nothing. You are quite aware of it.
  Hanno is waiting at the foot of the cellar stair. He regards you for a long moment, and then he holds out a small tablet and a sealed jar.
  "Oil," he says. "From Etruria. Old stock. A woman in the Subura will buy all you can find, and I told her you would." It is not an accusation. It is possibly the kindest thing he has ever done.
  $ do earn(-4)
  ?if can_invest("rome.wine")
    $ do invest("rome.wine")
    $ _deals += 1
    $ b1.collis_start = "wine"
  ?end
?end
?if must_feed()
  ~> feed_tonight
?end
-> naming

# feed_tonight
The day has taken more than you knew. You become aware of the hunger as a kind of fog, thickening along the edges of the lamp.
?if b1.cup == "accepted"
  The cup room is empty at this hour, but the laundress is there, as if she had been waiting. She holds out her arm without speaking.
  $ do feed("donor")
?elif b1.cup == "refused"
  You go to the river and the cattle pens, and it is a dull and thin meal. You eat it anyway.
  $ do feed("animal")
?else
  You go out in the dark and find a drunk asleep behind a wine shop, and you do not take long about it, and you do not leave him to die.
  $ do feed("human")
  $ secrecy -= 1
?end
